  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nHere is a contrived demonstration of the current behavior:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<button>focus me</button>\n<script>\nconst button = document.querySelector('button');\nbutton.addEventListener('focus', () => {\n  setTimeout(() => {\n    button.disabled = true;\n    button.textContent = 'disabled!';\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      button.disabled = false;\n      button.textContent = 'focus me';\n    }, 2000);\n  }, 1000);\n});\n</script>\n```\n\nA real example of why this behavior is bad is when setting disabled on a submit button while a form submits, unexpectedly moving focus is bad. It seems that we have a11y feedback that allowing focus to stay here would be good.\n\nI'm not sure how hard it would be to implent this or if it would break any invariants, but its probably implementable.\n\n@keithamus @aardrian @smhigley",
